  "id": "COMPOUND:29645 - PROTEIN:5794",
  "verbalization": "Caryptoside is shown to have a target relationship with LAPC4 through multiple pathways, with the strongest evidence linking it to LAPC4 via the compound 2-[4-[3-(3,4-Dimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan-6-yl]-3-methoxyphenoxy]-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxane-3,4,5-triol. This compound is identified as a target of LAPC4, and the final score of 0.5046 suggests a plausible mechanistic connection. Additionally, Caryptoside is linked to Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which is also a target of multiple compounds, including 2-Nonyl-4-hydroxyquinoline N-oxide and [(3S,10S,13R,17R)-17-(5-ethyl-6-methylhept-6-en-2-yl)-4,10,13,14-tetramethyl-1,2,3,4,5,6,9,11,12,15,16,17-dodecahydrocyclopenta[a]phenanthren-3-yl] acetate, all of which are also targets of LAPC4. These findings suggest that Caryptoside may act through a common pathway involving Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which is a key regulator of cellular signaling and may influence LAPC4 function. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Caryptoside could modulate LAPC4 activity, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact nature of the interaction.",
